      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm. Like you said, it\u0027s only used by particles, although that\u0027s really because particles is the only user of generic-program SkSL. We have some unit tests, but those either don\u0027t use uniforms, or know the layout implicitly. In any case, I agree it doesn\u0027t belong in the SkVM code (the logic will likely remain identical if/when we support generic programs with the RP code generator), but I\u0027m also not convinced it\u0027s particles-only. I think an even better end result would be having this code in SkSL::Program like this, but sharing the logic with the existing code in SkRuntimeEffect that does the ~same thing (to a slightly different format).\n\nI think it\u0027s okay to land this, but I\u0027d add a comment that the information being returned is really about rte/generic programs, not about uniforms for fragment or vertex shaders (where there are going to be opaque types missing, etc).",
